※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=42 diag=none

※ What a `break` hands over goes to the loop it names, not to the loop it
※ stands in -- which is the same rule the jump itself follows, and is what
※ makes a search of two dimensions one expression.
※
※ Every way a loop can be left gives one type: every `break` naming it and its
※ `else` arm alike.  The block the loop ends at is reached down all of those
※ ways and reads one thing, so there is one type for that thing to have.

fn cell_where(product: u6) → u6:
    foreach §rows r := 1u6…5u6:
        foreach c := 1u6…5u6:
            if r × c = product:
                ※ hands the outer loop its value from inside the inner one
                break §rows r × 10u6 + c
    else:
        0u6

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ※ 2 × 3 is the first pair found, so 23; and nothing makes 29
    cell_where(6u6) + cell_where(29u6) + 19u6
